        "text": "Josh Lowenthal represents the 69th District in the California State Assembly, elected in 2022. He is a small-business owner in tech and a former teacher. In the Assembly, he wrote AB 2 to allow fines up to $1 million per child when a tech platform's negligence causes harm. He also co-introduced a bill to bar social media platforms from allowing users under 16 to create or maintain accounts. His campaign says he wants to build more housing, grow the economy, and cut red tape. In 2025, he supported temporarily suspending the state's independent redistricting commission.",
